{%- comment -%}
  Authorization policy: test_principal_member (Layer-2, app-owned; TEST fixture).

  Permits a tool only when the calling PRINCIPAL (the bearer's user, not the browser
  session) has an ACTIVE mcp_access row with role user or admin — i.e. an approved
  member. Unlike the shipped `members_can_write` (which allows any authenticated
  caller), this actually distinguishes an approved member from a bare token holder,
  so the coverage suite can prove per-principal tool visibility and authz-deny.

  Fail-closed: no row, non-active status, or a lookup error → deny.
  Contract: return { allow, reason }. Receives principal, agent, arguments, tool,
  delegation_mode.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign r = '{}' | parse_json
  assign allow = false
  assign uid = principal.user_id | append: ''
  graphql g = 'modules/mcp/access/for_user', user_id: uid
  assign rec = g.records.results.first
  if rec != blank
    if rec.status == 'active'
      if rec.role == 'user' or rec.role == 'admin'
        assign allow = true
      endif
    endif
  endif
  hash_assign r['allow'] = allow
  if allow
    hash_assign r['reason'] = 'member'
  else
    hash_assign r['reason'] = 'not_member'
  endif
  return r
%}
